issue(id="0017" status="review")
  title Publish a native npm package for the CLI and HTML to Pug converter
  user-story
    as-a JavaScript or web-tooling user
    i-want to install puggers from npm and call the HTML to Pug converter from Node
    so-that Node workflows can use the converter through either a CLI or a typed runtime API
  premise.
    The Rust HTML importer is useful beyond the Cargo CLI, and npm users should
    be able to install a package named `puggers` that exposes both a command and
    a runtime converter. The first npm package should follow the native package
    pattern used by tools like dprint: a small top-level package plus
    platform-specific optional dependencies. The JavaScript package should be
    ESM-only, authored in TypeScript, built with tsdown, and shipped with
    generated `.d.ts` files. Browser and bundler-oriented wasm support is a
    separate future task, not an implicit promise of this Node package.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Add an npm-consumable `packages/puggers` package that exposes a typed ESM `convertHtmlToPug` function for Node.
    criterion Add a native Node-API crate that reuses `puggers-core` for conversion instead of maintaining JavaScript conversion logic.
    criterion Add an npm CLI bin that forwards to the native Rust `puggers` executable instead of duplicating CLI option parsing in JavaScript.
    criterion Support a repeatable native package build path for the current host target and document how platform-specific packages are generated.
    criterion Document that browser bundlers and wasm support are out of scope for this first npm package.
    criterion Reuse the existing Rust converter behavior and options rather than maintaining a separate JavaScript conversion implementation.
    criterion Add focused tests or examples that call the JavaScript API and assert converted Pug output for representative HTML input.
    criterion Add a repeatable build command for producing the native npm artifact, and make sure it can be run from a clean checkout with documented prerequisites.
    criterion Document the initial JavaScript API, native package resolution model, option mapping, and known platform limitations.
    criterion Add a Knope change file using `default` frontmatter that summarizes the new native npm converter surface.
  review-items
    item(status="covered") Use a dedicated top-level npm package named `puggers`, with platform-specific native packages under `@puggers/<target>`.
    item(status="covered") Use a native Node-API addon instead of wasm for the first Node package, so the converter keeps the same `puggers-core` parser path.
    item(status="covered") Leave browser and bundler-oriented wasm coverage to a follow-up task.
